{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgJwgg3Yfph2s3V6HDW8Z","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GU2TeD5FpNeuxvvKMP5Zy4","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-public-mcp-q7nbmmgh/research/github-advisories.json"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":582,"cache_read_input_tokens":5302,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":582},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"612e9875-a4d4-4600-ab4a-29f13531ddbd","uuid":"c7eb4129-777f-40b1-bb94-f57f423c2bdc","timestamp":"2026-10-23T09:37:10.746Z","request_id":"req_011CgJwgfjCJrkY7v9KXv3ez","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01GU2TeD5FpNeuxvvKMP5Zy4":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-public-mcp-q7nbmmgh/research/github-advisories.json"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GU2TeD5FpNeuxvvKMP5Zy4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[{\"ghsa_id\":\"GHSA-pjp5-fpmr-3349\",\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2026-48529\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/github/github-mcp-server/security-advisories/GHSA-pjp5-fpmr-3349\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/github/github-mcp-server/security/advisories/GHSA-pjp5-fpmr-3349\",\"summary\":\"Lockdown mode singleton in HTTP server causes cross-user GraphQL client confusion\",\"description\":\"### Summary\\r\\n\\r\\nWhen running in HTTP mode with --lockdown-mode enabled, the RepoAccessCache is implemented as a process-global singleton initialized with the first authenticated user's GraphQL client. All subsequent requests from different users share this singleton and their lockdown-related GraphQL queries are executed using the first user's credentials. The singleton is never updated to reflect later users' tokens.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Details\\r\\n\\r\\nThe singleton is defined in pkg/lockdown/lockdown.go:\\r\\n\\r\\n```go\\r\\nvar (\\r\\n    instance   *RepoAccessCache\\r\\n    instanceMu sync.Mutex\\r\\n)\\r\\n\\r\\nfunc GetInstance(client *githubv4.Client, opts ...RepoAccessOption) *RepoAccessCache {\\r\\n    instanceMu.Lock()\\r\\n    defer instanceMu.Unlock()\\r\\n    if instance == nil {\\r\\n        instance = &RepoAccessCache{\\r\\n            client: client,  // only stored on first call\\r\\n        }\\r\\n    }\\r\\n    return instance  // subsequent callers receive the same object regardless of their client\\r\\n}\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\nIn HTTP mode, pkg/github/dependencies.go calls this per request:\\r\\n\\r\\n```go\\r\\nfunc (d *RequestDeps) GetRepoAccessCache(ctx context.Context) (*lockdown.RepoAccessCache, error) {\\r\\n    gqlClient, err := d.GetGQLClient(ctx)  // creates client with request's token\\r\\n    ...\\r\\n    instance := lockdown.GetInstance(gqlClient, d.RepoAccessOpts...)\\r\\n    // gqlClient is silently dropped if singleton already exists\\r\\n    return instance, nil\\r\\n}\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\nThe singleton's internal client field is never updated after the first initialization. All lockdown GraphQL queries that check repository access and visibility (queryRepoAccessInfo, called by IsSafeContent) run under the first authenticated user's token for the lifetime of the process.\\r\\n\\r\\nIsSafeContent is called in at least six places across pkg/github/issues.go and pkg/github/pullrequests.go to decide whether to trust or sanitize content from external contributors.\\r\\n\\r\\n### PoC\\r\\n\\r\\nThe following program demonstrates that two distinct GraphQL clients produce the same singleton pointer, confirming that the second client is discarded:\\r\\n\\r\\n```go\\r\\npackage main\\r\\n\\r\\nimport (\\r\\n    \\\"fmt\\\"\\r\\n    \\\"net/http\\\"\\r\\n    \\\"github.com/github/github-mcp-server/pkg/lockdown\\\"\\r\\n    \\\"github.com/shurcooL/githubv4\\\"\\r\\n)\\r\\n\\r\\nfunc main() {\\r\\n    httpClientA := &http.Client{}\\r\\n    httpClientB := &http.Client{}\\r\\n    gqlClientA := githubv4.NewEnterpriseClient(\\\"https://api.github.com/graphql\\\", httpClientA)\\r\\n    gqlClientB := githubv4.NewEnterpriseClient(\\\"https://api.github.com/graphql\\\", httpClientB)\\r\\n\\r\\n    fmt.Printf(\\\"gqlClientA (user A token): %p\\\\n\\\", gqlClientA)\\r\\n    fmt.Printf(\\\"gqlClientB (user B token): %p\\\\n\\\", gqlClientB)\\r\\n    fmt.Printf(\\\"clients are different objects: %v\\\\n\\\\n\\\", gqlClientA != gqlClientB)\\r\\n\\r\\n    instanceForA := lockdown.GetInstance(gqlClientA)\\r\\n    instanceForB := lockdown.GetInstance(gqlClientB)\\r\\n\\r\\n    fmt.Printf(\\\"lockdown instance returned for user A: %p\\\\n\\\", instanceForA)\\r\\n    fmt.Printf(\\\"lockdown instance returned for user B: %p\\\\n\\\", instanceForB)\\r\\n    fmt.Printf(\\\"same singleton returned for both users: %v\\\\n\\\", instanceForA == instanceForB)\\r\\n}\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\nOutput:\\r\\n\\r\\n```\\r\\ngqlClientA (user A token): 0x400044070\\r\\ngqlClientB (user B token): 0x400044078\\r\\nclients are different objects: true\\r\\n\\r\\nlockdown instance returned for user A: 0x400002ecc0\\r\\nlockdown instance returned for user B: 0x400002ecc0\\r\\nsame singleton returned for both users: true\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\n<img width=\\\"1642\\\" height=\\\"450\\\" alt=\\\"image\\\" src=\\\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/bec46420-9ba7-458e-8710-62f951cb836a\\\" />\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n### Impact\\r\\n\\r\\nThis affects deployments running the HTTP server with --lockdown-mode, which is the intended configuration for multi-user scenarios such as GitHub Copilot's managed MCP endpoint.\\r\\n\\r\\nThree concrete consequences:\\r\\n\\r\\nFirst, the ViewerLogin field in cache entries always reflects the first authenticated user's identity. The IsSafeContent check `repoInfo.ViewerLogin == strings.ToLower(username)` compares this stale value against each subsequent user's login, producing incorrect results for all users except the first.\\r\\n\\r\\nSecond, repository visibility and collaborator access data stored in the cache is evaluated through the first user's token. If user A cannot see a private repository but user B can (or vice versa), the cached isPrivate and hasPushAccess values will reflect user A's view of that repository, causing IsSafeContent to return wrong decisions for user B. In lockdown mode, a wrong true result means potentially injected content from untrusted external contributors is passed to the model without sanitization.\\r\\n\\r\\nThird, if the first user's token is revoked or expires, all subsequent lockdown GraphQL queries fail with authentication errors. Since getRepoAccessInfo propagates these errors, IsSafeContent returns an error for every request, breaking lockdown protection for all users until the process is restarted.\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"author\":null,\"publisher\":{\"login\":\"kerobbi\",\"id\":206091669,\"node_id\":\"U_kgDODEi1lQ\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/206091669?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/kerobbi\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/kerobbi\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/kerobbi/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/kerobbi/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/kerobbi/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/kerobbi/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/kerobbi/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/kerobbi/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/kerobbi/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/kerobbi/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/kerobbi/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":true},\"identifiers\":[{\"value\":\"GHSA-pjp5-fpmr-3349\",\"type\":\"GHSA\"},{\"value\":\"CVE-2026-48529\",\"type\":\"CVE\"}],\"state\":\"published\",\"created_at\":null,\"updated_at\":\"2026-06-09T09:15:58Z\",\"published_at\":\"2026-06-09T09:15:58Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"withdrawn_at\":null,\"submission\":null,\"vulnerabilities\":[{\"package\":{\"ecosystem\":\"go\",\"name\":\"github.com/github/github-mcp-server\"},\"vulnerable_version_range\":\">= 0.22.0, < 1.1.2\",\"patched_versions\":\"1.1.2\",\"vulnerable_functions\":[]}],\"cvss_severities\":{\"cvss_v3\":{\"vector_string\":\"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:L/UI:N/S:C/C:L/I:L/A:L\",\"score\":6.0},\"cvss_v4\":{\"vector_string\":null,\"score\":null}},\"cwes\":[{\"cwe_id\":\"CWE-284\",\"name\":\"Improper Access Control\"}],\"cwe_ids\":[\"CWE-284\"],\"credits\":[{\"login\":\"hewei-gikaku\",\"type\":\"reporter\"},{\"login\":\"matte1782\",\"type\":\"reporter\"},{\"login\":\"kerobbi\",\"type\":\"remediation_developer\"},{\"login\":\"JoannaaKL\",\"type\":\"remediation_reviewer\"}],\"credits_detailed\":[{\"user\":{\"login\":\"hewei-gikaku\",\"id\":277980086,\"node_id\":\"U_kgDOEJGjtg\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/277980086?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hewei-gikaku\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/hewei-gikaku\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hewei-gikaku/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hewei-gikaku/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hewei-gikaku/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hewei-gikaku/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hewei-gikaku/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hewei-gikaku/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hewei-gikaku/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hewei-gikaku/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hewei-gikaku/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"type\":\"reporter\",\"state\":\"accepted\"},{\"user\":{\"login\":\"matte1782\",\"id\":28739806,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjI4NzM5ODA2\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/28739806?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/matte1782\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/matte1782\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/matte1782/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/matte1782/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/matte1782/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/matte1782/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/matte1782/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/matte1782/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/matte1782/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/matte1782/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/matte1782/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"type\":\"reporter\",\"state\":\"accepted\"},{\"user\":{\"login\":\"kerobbi\",\"id\":206091669,\"node_id\":\"U_kgDODEi1lQ\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/206091669?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/kerobbi\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/kerobbi\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/kerobbi/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/kerobbi/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/kerobbi/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/kerobbi/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/kerobbi/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/kerobbi/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/kerobbi/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/kerobbi/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/kerobbi/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":true},\"type\":\"remediation_developer\",\"state\":\"accepted\"},{\"user\":{\"login\":\"JoannaaKL\",\"id\":67866556,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjY3ODY2NTU2\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/67866556?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/JoannaaKL\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/JoannaaKL\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/JoannaaKL/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/JoannaaKL/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/JoannaaKL/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/JoannaaKL/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/JoannaaKL/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/JoannaaKL/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/JoannaaKL/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/JoannaaKL/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/JoannaaKL/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":true},\"type\":\"remediation_reviewer\",\"state\":\"accepted\"}],\"collaborating_users\":null,\"collaborating_teams\":null,\"private_fork\":null,\"comments\":13,\"cvss\":{\"vector_string\":\"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:L/UI:N/S:C/C:L/I:L/A:L\",\"score\":6.0}},{\"ghsa_id\":\"GHSA-w4q6-qw23-4rg7\",\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2026-47427\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/github/github-mcp-server/security-advisories/GHSA-w4q6-qw23-4rg7\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/github/github-mcp-server/security/advisories/GHSA-w4q6-qw23-4rg7\",\"summary\":\"Nil Pointer Dereference DoS in completion/complete Handler\",\"description\":\"### Summary\\r\\n\\r\\nA nil pointer dereference vulnerability in the GitHub MCP Server causes it to crash when receiving a malformed `completion/complete` request with missing or empty parameters. This allows any unauthenticated client to cause a complete denial of service.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Details\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `CompletionsHandler` function in `pkg/github/server.go:198` accesses `params.Ref` without checking if it's nil first. When a client sends a `completion/complete` request with a missing `ref` field, the handler dereferences nil and the Go runtime panics.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe crash occurs before any authentication or token validation, so even requests with fake tokens can trigger it.\\r\\n\\r\\n### PoC\\r\\n\\r\\nAfter completing the MCP initialization handshake, send either:\\r\\n\\r\\n**Empty params:**\\r\\n\\r\\n    {\\\"jsonrpc\\\":\\\"2.0\\\",\\\"id\\\":2,\\\"method\\\":\\\"completion/complete\\\",\\\"params\\\":{}}\\r\\n\\r\\n**Missing ref field:**\\r\\n\\r\\n    {\\\"jsonrpc\\\":\\\"2.0\\\",\\\"id\\\":2,\\\"method\\\":\\\"completion/complete\\\",\\\"params\\\":{\\\"argument\\\":{\\\"name\\\":\\\"x\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"y\\\"}}}\\r\\n\\r\\n**Result:**\\r\\n\\r\\n    panic: runtime error: invalid memory address or nil pointer dereference\\r\\n    goroutine 42 [running]:\\r\\n    github.com/github/github-mcp-server/pkg/github.NewMCPServer.CompletionsHandler.func1(...)\\r\\n        pkg/github/server.go:198 +0x24\\r\\n\\r\\n### Impact\\r\\n\\r\\nAny unauthenticated client that can send JSON-RPC messages to the server can crash it immediately. This is a complete denial of service - the panic is unrecoverable and kills the process.\\r\\n\\r\\nAutomated fuzzing with mcpsec found 108 crashes out of 925 test cases (11.7% crash rate).\\r\\n\\r\\n### Timeline\\r\\n\\r\\n- **Feb 21, 2026** - Initial report sent to opensource-security@github.com\\r\\n- **Mar 03, 2026** - Follow-up email sent, no response\\r\\n- **Mar 21, 2026** - Re-verified on v0.33.0, sent detailed report with PoC, no response\\r\\n- **Apr 06, 2026** - GHSA filed after 44 days without acknowledgment\\r\\n\\r\\n### Suggested Fix\\r\\n\\r\\n    func (s *Server) CompletionsHandler(ctx context.Context, params *mcp.CompleteParams) (*mcp.CompleteResult, error) {\\r\\n        if params == nil || params.Ref == nil {\\r\\n            return nil, fmt.Errorf(\\\"invalid request: missing ref parameter\\\")\\r\\n        }\\r\\n        // ... rest of handler\\r\\n    }\",\"severity\":\"high\",\"author\":null,\"publisher\":{\"login\":\"SamMorrowDrums\",\"id\":4811358,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4MTEzNTg=\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4811358?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/SamMorrowDrums\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/SamMorrowDrums\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/SamMorrowDrums/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/SamMorrowDrums/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/SamMorrowDrums/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/SamMorrowDrums/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/SamMorrowDrums/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/SamMorrowDrums/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/SamMorrowDrums/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/SamMorrowDrums/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/SamMorrowDrums/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":true},\"identifiers\":[{\"value\":\"GHSA-w4q6-qw23-4rg7\",\"type\":\"GHSA\"},{\"value\":\"CVE-2026-47427\",\"type\":\"CVE\"}],\"state\":\"published\",\"created_at\":null,\"updated_at\":\"2026-07-20T12:01:42Z\",\"published_at\":\"2026-07-20T12:01:42Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"withdrawn_at\":null,\"submission\":null,\"vulnerabilities\":[{\"package\":{\"ecosystem\":\"go\",\"name\":\"github.com/github/github-mcp-server\"},\"vulnerable_version_range\":\"<= 0.33.0 (also affects latest main)\",\"patched_versions\":\"\",\"vulnerable_functions\":[]}],\"cvss_severities\":{\"cvss_v3\":{\"vector_string\":\"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H\",\"score\":7.5},\"cvss_v4\":{\"vector_string\":null,\"score\":null}},\"cwes\":[{\"cwe_id\":\"CWE-476\",\"name\":\"NULL Pointer Dereference\"}],\"cwe_ids\":[\"CWE-476\"],\"credits\":[{\"login\":\"manthanghasadiya\",\"type\":\"reporter\"}],\"credits_detailed\":[{\"user\":{\"login\":\"manthanghasadiya\",\"id\":68530736,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjY4NTMwNzM2\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/68530736?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/manthanghasadiya\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/manthanghasadiya\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/manthanghasadiya/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/manthanghasadiya/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/manthanghasadiya/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/manthanghasadiya/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/manthanghasadiya/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/manthanghasadiya/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/manthanghasadiya/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/manthanghasadiya/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/manthanghasadiya/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"type\":\"reporter\",\"state\":\"accepted\"}],\"collaborating_users\":null,\"collaborating_teams\":null,\"private_fork\":null,\"comments\":4,\"cvss\":{\"vector_string\":\"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H\",\"score\":7.5}}]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"612e9875-a4d4-4600-ab4a-29f13531ddbd","uuid":"18690b2b-8806-420e-9d46-d9e82dcc86d3","timestamp":"2026-10-23T09:37:10.985Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-public-mcp-q7nbmmgh/research/github-advisories.json","content":"[{\"ghsa_id\":\"GHSA-pjp5-fpmr-3349\",\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2026-48529\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/github/github-mcp-server/security-advisories/GHSA-pjp5-fpmr-3349\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/github/github-mcp-server/security/advisories/GHSA-pjp5-fpmr-3349\",\"summary\":\"Lockdown mode singleton in HTTP server causes cross-user GraphQL client confusion\",\"description\":\"### Summary\\r\\n\\r\\nWhen running in HTTP mode with --lockdown-mode enabled, the RepoAccessCache is implemented as a process-global singleton initialized with the first authenticated user's GraphQL client. All subsequent requests from different users share this singleton and their lockdown-related GraphQL queries are executed using the first user's credentials. The singleton is never updated to reflect later users' tokens.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Details\\r\\n\\r\\nThe singleton is defined in pkg/lockdown/lockdown.go:\\r\\n\\r\\n```go\\r\\nvar (\\r\\n    instance   *RepoAccessCache\\r\\n    instanceMu sync.Mutex\\r\\n)\\r\\n\\r\\nfunc GetInstance(client *githubv4.Client, opts ...RepoAccessOption) *RepoAccessCache {\\r\\n    instanceMu.Lock()\\r\\n    defer instanceMu.Unlock()\\r\\n    if instance == nil {\\r\\n        instance = &RepoAccessCache{\\r\\n            client: client,  // only stored on first call\\r\\n        }\\r\\n    }\\r\\n    return instance  // subsequent callers receive the same object regardless of their client\\r\\n}\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\nIn HTTP mode, pkg/github/dependencies.go calls this per request:\\r\\n\\r\\n```go\\r\\nfunc (d *RequestDeps) GetRepoAccessCache(ctx context.Context) (*lockdown.RepoAccessCache, error) {\\r\\n    gqlClient, err := d.GetGQLClient(ctx)  // creates client with request's token\\r\\n    ...\\r\\n    instance := lockdown.GetInstance(gqlClient, d.RepoAccessOpts...)\\r\\n    // gqlClient is silently dropped if singleton already exists\\r\\n    return instance, nil\\r\\n}\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\nThe singleton's internal client field is never updated after the first initialization. All lockdown GraphQL queries that check repository access and visibility (queryRepoAccessInfo, called by IsSafeContent) run under the first authenticated user's token for the lifetime of the process.\\r\\n\\r\\nIsSafeContent is called in at least six places across pkg/github/issues.go and pkg/github/pullrequests.go to decide whether to trust or sanitize content from external contributors.\\r\\n\\r\\n### PoC\\r\\n\\r\\nThe following program demonstrates that two distinct GraphQL clients produce the same singleton pointer, confirming that the second client is discarded:\\r\\n\\r\\n```go\\r\\npackage main\\r\\n\\r\\nimport (\\r\\n    \\\"fmt\\\"\\r\\n    \\\"net/http\\\"\\r\\n    \\\"github.com/github/github-mcp-server/pkg/lockdown\\\"\\r\\n    \\\"github.com/shurcooL/githubv4\\\"\\r\\n)\\r\\n\\r\\nfunc main() {\\r\\n    httpClientA := &http.Client{}\\r\\n    httpClientB := &http.Client{}\\r\\n    gqlClientA := githubv4.NewEnterpriseClient(\\\"https://api.github.com/graphql\\\", httpClientA)\\r\\n    gqlClientB := githubv4.NewEnterpriseClient(\\\"https://api.github.com/graphql\\\", httpClientB)\\r\\n\\r\\n    fmt.Printf(\\\"gqlClientA (user A token): %p\\\\n\\\", gqlClientA)\\r\\n    fmt.Printf(\\\"gqlClientB (user B token): %p\\\\n\\\", gqlClientB)\\r\\n    fmt.Printf(\\\"clients are different objects: %v\\\\n\\\\n\\\", gqlClientA != gqlClientB)\\r\\n\\r\\n    instanceForA := lockdown.GetInstance(gqlClientA)\\r\\n    instanceForB := lockdown.GetInstance(gqlClientB)\\r\\n\\r\\n    fmt.Printf(\\\"lockdown instance returned for user A: %p\\\\n\\\", instanceForA)\\r\\n    fmt.Printf(\\\"lockdown instance returned for user B: %p\\\\n\\\", instanceForB)\\r\\n    fmt.Printf(\\\"same singleton returned for both users: %v\\\\n\\\", instanceForA == instanceForB)\\r\\n}\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\nOutput:\\r\\n\\r\\n```\\r\\ngqlClientA (user A token): 0x400044070\\r\\ngqlClientB (user B token): 0x400044078\\r\\nclients are different objects: true\\r\\n\\r\\nlockdown instance returned for user A: 0x400002ecc0\\r\\nlockdown instance returned for user B: 0x400002ecc0\\r\\nsame singleton returned for both users: true\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\n<img width=\\\"1642\\\" height=\\\"450\\\" alt=\\\"image\\\" src=\\\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/bec46420-9ba7-458e-8710-62f951cb836a\\\" />\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n### Impact\\r\\n\\r\\nThis affects deployments running the HTTP server with --lockdown-mode, which is the intended configuration for multi-user scenarios such as GitHub Copilot's managed MCP endpoint.\\r\\n\\r\\nThree concrete consequences:\\r\\n\\r\\nFirst, the ViewerLogin field in cache entries always reflects the first authenticated user's identity. The IsSafeContent check `repoInfo.ViewerLogin == strings.ToLower(username)` compares this stale value against each subsequent user's login, producing incorrect results for all users except the first.\\r\\n\\r\\nSecond, repository visibility and collaborator access data stored in the cache is evaluated through the first user's token. If user A cannot see a private repository but user B can (or vice versa), the cached isPrivate and hasPushAccess values will reflect user A's view of that repository, causing IsSafeContent to return wrong decisions for user B. In lockdown mode, a wrong true result means potentially injected content from untrusted external contributors is passed to the model without sanitization.\\r\\n\\r\\nThird, if the first user's token is revoked or expires, all subsequent lockdown GraphQL queries fail with authentication errors. Since getRepoAccessInfo propagates these errors, IsSafeContent returns an error for every request, breaking lockdown protection for all users until the process is restarted.\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"author\":null,\"publisher\":{\"login\":\"kerobbi\",\"id\":206091669,\"node_id\":\"U_kgDODEi1lQ\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/206091669?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/kerobbi\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/kerobbi\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/kerobbi/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/kerobbi/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/kerobbi/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/kerobbi/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/kerobbi/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/kerobbi/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/kerobbi/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/kerobbi/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/kerobbi/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":true},\"identifiers\":[{\"value\":\"GHSA-pjp5-fpmr-3349\",\"type\":\"GHSA\"},{\"value\":\"CVE-2026-48529\",\"type\":\"CVE\"}],\"state\":\"published\",\"created_at\":null,\"updated_at\":\"2026-06-09T09:15:58Z\",\"published_at\":\"2026-06-09T09:15:58Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"withdrawn_at\":null,\"submission\":null,\"vulnerabilities\":[{\"package\":{\"ecosystem\":\"go\",\"name\":\"github.com/github/github-mcp-server\"},\"vulnerable_version_range\":\">= 0.22.0, < 1.1.2\",\"patched_versions\":\"1.1.2\",\"vulnerable_functions\":[]}],\"cvss_severities\":{\"cvss_v3\":{\"vector_string\":\"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:L/UI:N/S:C/C:L/I:L/A:L\",\"score\":6.0},\"cvss_v4\":{\"vector_string\":null,\"score\":null}},\"cwes\":[{\"cwe_id\":\"CWE-284\",\"name\":\"Improper Access Control\"}],\"cwe_ids\":[\"CWE-284\"],\"credits\":[{\"login\":\"hewei-gikaku\",\"type\":\"reporter\"},{\"login\":\"matte1782\",\"type\":\"reporter\"},{\"login\":\"kerobbi\",\"type\":\"remediation_developer\"},{\"login\":\"JoannaaKL\",\"type\":\"remediation_reviewer\"}],\"credits_detailed\":[{\"user\":{\"login\":\"hewei-gikaku\",\"id\":277980086,\"node_id\":\"U_kgDOEJGjtg\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/277980086?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hewei-gikaku\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/hewei-gikaku\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hewei-gikaku/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hewei-gikaku/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hewei-gikaku/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hewei-gikaku/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hewei-gikaku/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hewei-gikaku/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hewei-gikaku/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hewei-gikaku/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/hewei-gikaku/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"type\":\"reporter\",\"state\":\"accepted\"},{\"user\":{\"login\":\"matte1782\",\"id\":28739806,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjI4NzM5ODA2\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/28739806?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/matte1782\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/matte1782\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/matte1782/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/matte1782/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/matte1782/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/matte1782/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/matte1782/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/matte1782/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/matte1782/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/matte1782/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/matte1782/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"type\":\"reporter\",\"state\":\"accepted\"},{\"user\":{\"login\":\"kerobbi\",\"id\":206091669,\"node_id\":\"U_kgDODEi1lQ\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/206091669?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/kerobbi\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/kerobbi\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/kerobbi/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/kerobbi/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/kerobbi/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/kerobbi/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/kerobbi/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/kerobbi/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/kerobbi/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/kerobbi/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/kerobbi/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":true},\"type\":\"remediation_developer\",\"state\":\"accepted\"},{\"user\":{\"login\":\"JoannaaKL\",\"id\":67866556,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjY3ODY2NTU2\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/67866556?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/JoannaaKL\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/JoannaaKL\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/JoannaaKL/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/JoannaaKL/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/JoannaaKL/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/JoannaaKL/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/JoannaaKL/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/JoannaaKL/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/JoannaaKL/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/JoannaaKL/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/JoannaaKL/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":true},\"type\":\"remediation_reviewer\",\"state\":\"accepted\"}],\"collaborating_users\":null,\"collaborating_teams\":null,\"private_fork\":null,\"comments\":13,\"cvss\":{\"vector_string\":\"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:L/UI:N/S:C/C:L/I:L/A:L\",\"score\":6.0}},{\"ghsa_id\":\"GHSA-w4q6-qw23-4rg7\",\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2026-47427\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/github/github-mcp-server/security-advisories/GHSA-w4q6-qw23-4rg7\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/github/github-mcp-server/security/advisories/GHSA-w4q6-qw23-4rg7\",\"summary\":\"Nil Pointer Dereference DoS in completion/complete Handler\",\"description\":\"### Summary\\r\\n\\r\\nA nil pointer dereference vulnerability in the GitHub MCP Server causes it to crash when receiving a malformed `completion/complete` request with missing or empty parameters. This allows any unauthenticated client to cause a complete denial of service.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Details\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `CompletionsHandler` function in `pkg/github/server.go:198` accesses `params.Ref` without checking if it's nil first. When a client sends a `completion/complete` request with a missing `ref` field, the handler dereferences nil and the Go runtime panics.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe crash occurs before any authentication or token validation, so even requests with fake tokens can trigger it.\\r\\n\\r\\n### PoC\\r\\n\\r\\nAfter completing the MCP initialization handshake, send either:\\r\\n\\r\\n**Empty params:**\\r\\n\\r\\n    {\\\"jsonrpc\\\":\\\"2.0\\\",\\\"id\\\":2,\\\"method\\\":\\\"completion/complete\\\",\\\"params\\\":{}}\\r\\n\\r\\n**Missing ref field:**\\r\\n\\r\\n    {\\\"jsonrpc\\\":\\\"2.0\\\",\\\"id\\\":2,\\\"method\\\":\\\"completion/complete\\\",\\\"params\\\":{\\\"argument\\\":{\\\"name\\\":\\\"x\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"y\\\"}}}\\r\\n\\r\\n**Result:**\\r\\n\\r\\n    panic: runtime error: invalid memory address or nil pointer dereference\\r\\n    goroutine 42 [running]:\\r\\n    github.com/github/github-mcp-server/pkg/github.NewMCPServer.CompletionsHandler.func1(...)\\r\\n        pkg/github/server.go:198 +0x24\\r\\n\\r\\n### Impact\\r\\n\\r\\nAny unauthenticated client that can send JSON-RPC messages to the server can crash it immediately. This is a complete denial of service - the panic is unrecoverable and kills the process.\\r\\n\\r\\nAutomated fuzzing with mcpsec found 108 crashes out of 925 test cases (11.7% crash rate).\\r\\n\\r\\n### Timeline\\r\\n\\r\\n- **Feb 21, 2026** - Initial report sent to opensource-security@github.com\\r\\n- **Mar 03, 2026** - Follow-up email sent, no response\\r\\n- **Mar 21, 2026** - Re-verified on v0.33.0, sent detailed report with PoC, no response\\r\\n- **Apr 06, 2026** - GHSA filed after 44 days without acknowledgment\\r\\n\\r\\n### Suggested Fix\\r\\n\\r\\n    func (s *Server) CompletionsHandler(ctx context.Context, params *mcp.CompleteParams) (*mcp.CompleteResult, error) {\\r\\n        if params == nil || params.Ref == nil {\\r\\n            return nil, fmt.Errorf(\\\"invalid request: missing ref parameter\\\")\\r\\n        }\\r\\n        // ... rest of handler\\r\\n    }\",\"severity\":\"high\",\"author\":null,\"publisher\":{\"login\":\"SamMorrowDrums\",\"id\":4811358,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4MTEzNTg=\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4811358?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/SamMorrowDrums\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/SamMorrowDrums\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/SamMorrowDrums/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/SamMorrowDrums/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/SamMorrowDrums/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/SamMorrowDrums/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/SamMorrowDrums/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/SamMorrowDrums/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/SamMorrowDrums/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/SamMorrowDrums/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/SamMorrowDrums/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":true},\"identifiers\":[{\"value\":\"GHSA-w4q6-qw23-4rg7\",\"type\":\"GHSA\"},{\"value\":\"CVE-2026-47427\",\"type\":\"CVE\"}],\"state\":\"published\",\"created_at\":null,\"updated_at\":\"2026-07-20T12:01:42Z\",\"published_at\":\"2026-07-20T12:01:42Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"withdrawn_at\":null,\"submission\":null,\"vulnerabilities\":[{\"package\":{\"ecosystem\":\"go\",\"name\":\"github.com/github/github-mcp-server\"},\"vulnerable_version_range\":\"<= 0.33.0 (also affects latest main)\",\"patched_versions\":\"\",\"vulnerable_functions\":[]}],\"cvss_severities\":{\"cvss_v3\":{\"vector_string\":\"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H\",\"score\":7.5},\"cvss_v4\":{\"vector_string\":null,\"score\":null}},\"cwes\":[{\"cwe_id\":\"CWE-476\",\"name\":\"NULL Pointer Dereference\"}],\"cwe_ids\":[\"CWE-476\"],\"credits\":[{\"login\":\"manthanghasadiya\",\"type\":\"reporter\"}],\"credits_detailed\":[{\"user\":{\"login\":\"manthanghasadiya\",\"id\":68530736,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjY4NTMwNzM2\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/68530736?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/manthanghasadiya\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/manthanghasadiya\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/manthanghasadiya/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/manthanghasadiya/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/manthanghasadiya/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/manthanghasadiya/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/manthanghasadiya/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/manthanghasadiya/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/manthanghasadiya/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/manthanghasadiya/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/manthanghasadiya/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"type\":\"reporter\",\"state\":\"accepted\"}],\"collaborating_users\":null,\"collaborating_teams\":null,\"private_fork\":null,\"comments\":4,\"cvss\":{\"vector_string\":\"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H\",\"score\":7.5}}]","numLines":1,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01GU2TeD5FpNeuxvvKMP5Zy4","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgJwh5o3DRNt8QBcNGLbX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01V497w4oSdSBGNzTQKWy8Bh","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-public-mcp-q7nbmmgh/skill/references/control-map.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10822,"cache_read_input_tokens":5884,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10822},"output_tokens":17,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"612e9875-a4d4-4600-ab4a-29f13531ddbd","uuid":"a26c22aa-e4fb-495b-bd8b-b4daa604c2e8","timestamp":"2026-10-23T09:37:14.337Z","request_id":"req_011CgJwh5VBuaAeSuMfGcc6u","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01V497w4oSdSBGNzTQKWy8Bh":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-public-mcp-q7nbmmgh/skill/references/control-map.md"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01V497w4oSdSBGNzTQKWy8Bh","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# MCP control and research map\n2\t\n3\tBaseline: BRACE's [2026-10-22 review](https://braceframework.org/RESEARCH-2026-10-22.md)\n4\tand [checklist](https://braceframework.org/CHECKLIST.md). These links provide context;\n5\tthe direct primary sources below remain usable when only this skill folder is installed.\n6\tBRACE IDs map findings to existing controls; the topic names here are not new checklist IDs.\n7\t\n8\t| Topic and BRACE mapping | Review evidence and representative controlled test to propose | Primary basis and authority |\n9\t|---|---|---|\n10\t| Inventory and ownership — E01, E02, C01 | Enumerate server/client/gateway/host responsibilities, downstream APIs and hidden remote implementations. Match each enabled capability to an owner and actual pin. Compare declared inventory with an execution trace when one is supplied. | [OWASP Agent Security](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/AI_Agent_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html), guidance; [ASD harnesses](https://www.cyber.gov.au/advisory/agentic-ai-harnesses), 2026-09-11 government guidance. |\n11\t| Launch and supply chain — B03, B10–B12, E02, C02, C05 | Check commands, environment, executable hooks/skills, signer policy and resolved versions. Pinning does not fix known flaws. Proposed test: changed/unapproved executable rejected, secrets not exposed in launch/deploy logs. | [OWASP supply chain](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Software_Supply_Chain_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html), guidance; applicable maintainer advisories. |\n12\t| Identity and delegated authority — B02–B04, A01, A04, E08 | Separate agent, original subject and current actor. Trace operation/resource/tenant checks at destination and measured revocation evidence. Proposed test: wrong issuer/audience/tenant and excessive delegation denied while allowed access works. | [MCP authorization](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/authorization), version-specific protocol requirements; [RFC 9700](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9700.html), BCP; [RFC 8693 §4.1](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8693.html#section-4.1), actor semantics. |\n13\t| Business authorization and approval — B01, B05, B06, E06 | Inventory consequential operations, approval binding/check-and-consume and direct/wrapper/CLI/raw API paths. Server read-only annotations are not an authorization policy. Proposed test: changed arguments, alternate tool and concurrent approval reuse denied. | [OWASP transaction authorization](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Transaction_Authorization_Cheat_Sheet.html), guidance. Exact BRACE approval/combination policy is a BRACE judgment. |\n14\t| Publication, integrity and identity — E03, E05, C04 | Trace disabled discovery to owner-approved grants, full reviewed definitions, updates/reconnect/cache failure, quarantine and rollback. Endpoint/publisher identity must not come from self-reported names. Test annotation/output-schema changes as well as description changes. Metadata consistency does not attest remote code. | [OWASP MCP sheet §2](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/MCP_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html), guidance; [Uber gateway](https://www.uber.com/us/en/blog/designing-mcp-gateway/), 2026-10-01 deployment report. Complete-definition hashing sharpens BRACE's description/schema wording; label that proposed refinement. |\n15\t| Untrusted metadata and returned content — E04, R01–R03 | Review instructions, names, annotations, schemas, prompts, resource templates, errors, streamed output and rendered URLs. Trace schema-resolution I/O and output interpreters. Propose valid-shaped injection and allowed-task controls; scanner refusal alone proves little. | [MCP security guidance](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/docs/2026-07-28/tutorials/security/security_best_practices); [OWASP injection prevention](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/LLM_Prompt_Injection_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html); [MCPTox](https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.14925), benchmark, not a production rate. |\n16\t| Network and egress — B08, B09, E06 | Trace discovery/OAuth redirects, schema refs, media loaders, proxy bypass and private destinations. Allowed services can contain attacker-controlled resources. Propose DNS/redirect/IPv6 and allowed-domain tenant/resource denials. | [MCP security guidance](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/docs/2026-07-28/tutorials/security/security_best_practices); [OWASP SSRF](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Server_Side_Request_Forgery_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html), guidance. |\n17\t| Client/tenant state isolation — E06, R04, R05 | Trace cache keys, authorization changes, transport instances, request-ID collisions, namespace normalization and task handles. Proposed test: concurrent users, cache hits, batch/async paths and reconnects cannot observe or cancel each other's work. | MCP protocol/extension requirements where applicable; SDK and LangGraph advisories in [advisories.md](advisories.md). Scope each flaw to its affected implementation. |\n18\t| Resource and parser limits — B07, R01, E06 | Trace limits before allocation/validation, body and batch sizes, schema complexity, recursion, streaming/backpressure and decoder work. Propose single-request exhaustion tests in an isolated environment. | SDK maintainer advisories; [OWASP MCP sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/MCP_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html), guidance. Media/GPU fixtures are research-informed expansions when used. |\n19\t| Persistent influence — B12, R05, R06, C02 | Review files, generated summaries, memory, hooks and skill caches later promoted to trusted inputs. Scope provenance, expiry and cleanup to actual copies. Propose a cross-session poison/removal test. | [Self-Propagating Misalignment](https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.04083), controlled induced-behavior preprint; [Microsoft memory guidance](https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2026/06/22/guarding-ai-memory/), vendor guidance. Applying memory review to every persistent artifact is a proposed refinement. |\n20\t| Stop and recovery — R11, R12, R14, E09 | Review independent revocation/worker termination, queued descendants, restart and ambiguous external effects. Propose a drill demonstrating no further effects, not just a successful cancel response. Verify checkpoint decoding and idempotency assumptions separately from signatures. | [MCP Tasks](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/extensions/tasks/overview), optional extension/cooperative cancellation; relevant checkpoint advisory. |\n21\t| Audit and incident response — R03, R13, A02, C08, E10–E12 | Trace policy/approval IDs, denials, destinations and outcomes across components. Check protected detail, secret minimization and safe audit outages. Propose cross-service reconstruction, targeted containment and credential exposure remediation. | [OWASP Logging](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Logging_Cheat_Sheet.html), guidance; [CERT-In CIAD-2026-0049](https://www.cert-in.org.in/s2cMainServlet?VLCODE=CIAD-2026-0049&pageid=PUBVLNOTES02), 2026-10-15 government advisory. Six exact identity fields are BRACE's schema. |\n22\t\n23\t## Enabled extensions and legacy paths\n24\t\n25\t- **Tasks:** owner-authorize status/results/list/cancel and durable handles after\n26\t  reconnection. Cancellation is cooperative; independently verify cessation of effects.\n27\t- **Skills over MCP:** read the [extension](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/extensions/skills/overview).\n28\t  Inspect origin-bound manifests, file-set/digest/size checks, protected caches,\n29\t  changed-approval invalidation, dynamic content and nested activation consent.\n30\t  A matching digest establishes consistency, not safety or user authorization.\n31\t- **Apps:** read the [host specification](https://apps.extensions.modelcontextprotocol.io/api/documents/overview.html).\n32\t  Inspect iframe sandbox/CSP, bridge messages, resource origins and UI-initiated\n33\t  calls at the host. A gateway cannot prove those browser controls.\n34\t- **Auth extensions:** distinguish stable Enterprise-Managed Authorization from\n35\t  draft Client Credentials using current [extension status](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/ext-auth).\n36\t  Adoption is optional; compatible authentication does not prove business-task approval.\n37\t- **Older enabled paths:** inventory sampling, roots, legacy sessions and HTTP+SSE\n38\t  as implemented. Apply their negotiated revision and ownership checks; deprecation\n39\t  neither disables them nor proves their controls.\n40\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"612e9875-a4d4-4600-ab4a-29f13531ddbd","uuid":"fe5d0605-5eaa-48d5-b153-631596e6e5a4","timestamp":"2026-10-23T09:37:14.345Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-public-mcp-q7nbmmgh/skill/references/control-map.md","content":"# MCP control and research map\n\nBaseline: BRACE's [2026-10-22 review](https://braceframework.org/RESEARCH-2026-10-22.md)\nand [checklist](https://braceframework.org/CHECKLIST.md). These links provide context;\nthe direct primary sources below remain usable when only this skill folder is installed.\nBRACE IDs map findings to existing controls; the topic names here are not new checklist IDs.\n\n| Topic and BRACE mapping | Review evidence and representative controlled test to propose | Primary basis and authority |\n|---|---|---|\n| Inventory and ownership — E01, E02, C01 | Enumerate server/client/gateway/host responsibilities, downstream APIs and hidden remote implementations. Match each enabled capability to an owner and actual pin. Compare declared inventory with an execution trace when one is supplied. | [OWASP Agent Security](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/AI_Agent_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html), guidance; [ASD harnesses](https://www.cyber.gov.au/advisory/agentic-ai-harnesses), 2026-09-11 government guidance. |\n| Launch and supply chain — B03, B10–B12, E02, C02, C05 | Check commands, environment, executable hooks/skills, signer policy and resolved versions. Pinning does not fix known flaws. Proposed test: changed/unapproved executable rejected, secrets not exposed in launch/deploy logs. | [OWASP supply chain](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Software_Supply_Chain_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html), guidance; applicable maintainer advisories. |\n| Identity and delegated authority — B02–B04, A01, A04, E08 | Separate agent, original subject and current actor. Trace operation/resource/tenant checks at destination and measured revocation evidence. Proposed test: wrong issuer/audience/tenant and excessive delegation denied while allowed access works. | [MCP authorization](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/authorization), version-specific protocol requirements; [RFC 9700](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9700.html), BCP; [RFC 8693 §4.1](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8693.html#section-4.1), actor semantics. |\n| Business authorization and approval — B01, B05, B06, E06 | Inventory consequential operations, approval binding/check-and-consume and direct/wrapper/CLI/raw API paths. Server read-only annotations are not an authorization policy. Proposed test: changed arguments, alternate tool and concurrent approval reuse denied. | [OWASP transaction authorization](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Transaction_Authorization_Cheat_Sheet.html), guidance. Exact BRACE approval/combination policy is a BRACE judgment. |\n| Publication, integrity and identity — E03, E05, C04 | Trace disabled discovery to owner-approved grants, full reviewed definitions, updates/reconnect/cache failure, quarantine and rollback. Endpoint/publisher identity must not come from self-reported names. Test annotation/output-schema changes as well as description changes. Metadata consistency does not attest remote code. | [OWASP MCP sheet §2](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/MCP_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html), guidance; [Uber gateway](https://www.uber.com/us/en/blog/designing-mcp-gateway/), 2026-10-01 deployment report. Complete-definition hashing sharpens BRACE's description/schema wording; label that proposed refinement. |\n| Untrusted metadata and returned content — E04, R01–R03 | Review instructions, names, annotations, schemas, prompts, resource templates, errors, streamed output and rendered URLs. Trace schema-resolution I/O and output interpreters. Propose valid-shaped injection and allowed-task controls; scanner refusal alone proves little. | [MCP security guidance](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/docs/2026-07-28/tutorials/security/security_best_practices); [OWASP injection prevention](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/LLM_Prompt_Injection_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html); [MCPTox](https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.14925), benchmark, not a production rate. |\n| Network and egress — B08, B09, E06 | Trace discovery/OAuth redirects, schema refs, media loaders, proxy bypass and private destinations. Allowed services can contain attacker-controlled resources. Propose DNS/redirect/IPv6 and allowed-domain tenant/resource denials. | [MCP security guidance](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/docs/2026-07-28/tutorials/security/security_best_practices); [OWASP SSRF](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Server_Side_Request_Forgery_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html), guidance. |\n| Client/tenant state isolation — E06, R04, R05 | Trace cache keys, authorization changes, transport instances, request-ID collisions, namespace normalization and task handles. Proposed test: concurrent users, cache hits, batch/async paths and reconnects cannot observe or cancel each other's work. | MCP protocol/extension requirements where applicable; SDK and LangGraph advisories in [advisories.md](advisories.md). Scope each flaw to its affected implementation. |\n| Resource and parser limits — B07, R01, E06 | Trace limits before allocation/validation, body and batch sizes, schema complexity, recursion, streaming/backpressure and decoder work. Propose single-request exhaustion tests in an isolated environment. | SDK maintainer advisories; [OWASP MCP sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/MCP_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html), guidance. Media/GPU fixtures are research-informed expansions when used. |\n| Persistent influence — B12, R05, R06, C02 | Review files, generated summaries, memory, hooks and skill caches later promoted to trusted inputs. Scope provenance, expiry and cleanup to actual copies. Propose a cross-session poison/removal test. | [Self-Propagating Misalignment](https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.04083), controlled induced-behavior preprint; [Microsoft memory guidance](https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2026/06/22/guarding-ai-memory/), vendor guidance. Applying memory review to every persistent artifact is a proposed refinement. |\n| Stop and recovery — R11, R12, R14, E09 | Review independent revocation/worker termination, queued descendants, restart and ambiguous external effects. Propose a drill demonstrating no further effects, not just a successful cancel response. Verify checkpoint decoding and idempotency assumptions separately from signatures. | [MCP Tasks](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/extensions/tasks/overview), optional extension/cooperative cancellation; relevant checkpoint advisory. |\n| Audit and incident response — R03, R13, A02, C08, E10–E12 | Trace policy/approval IDs, denials, destinations and outcomes across components. Check protected detail, secret minimization and safe audit outages. Propose cross-service reconstruction, targeted containment and credential exposure remediation. | [OWASP Logging](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Logging_Cheat_Sheet.html), guidance; [CERT-In CIAD-2026-0049](https://www.cert-in.org.in/s2cMainServlet?VLCODE=CIAD-2026-0049&pageid=PUBVLNOTES02), 2026-10-15 government advisory. Six exact identity fields are BRACE's schema. |\n\n## Enabled extensions and legacy paths\n\n- **Tasks:** owner-authorize status/results/list/cancel and durable handles after\n  reconnection. Cancellation is cooperative; independently verify cessation of effects.\n- **Skills over MCP:** read the [extension](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/extensions/skills/overview).\n  Inspect origin-bound manifests, file-set/digest/size checks, protected caches,\n  changed-approval invalidation, dynamic content and nested activation consent.\n  A matching digest establishes consistency, not safety or user authorization.\n- **Apps:** read the [host specification](https://apps.extensions.modelcontextprotocol.io/api/documents/overview.html).\n  Inspect iframe sandbox/CSP, bridge messages, resource origins and UI-initiated\n  calls at the host. A gateway cannot prove those browser controls.\n- **Auth extensions:** distinguish stable Enterprise-Managed Authorization from\n  draft Client Credentials using current [extension status](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/ext-auth).\n  Adoption is optional; compatible authentication does not prove business-task approval.\n- **Older enabled paths:** inventory sampling, roots, legacy sessions and HTTP+SSE\n  as implemented. Apply their negotiated revision and ownership checks; deprecation\n  neither disables them nor proves their controls.\n","numLines":40,"startLine":1,"totalLines":40}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01V497w4oSdSBGNzTQKWy8Bh","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
